DEFAULT PIV CREDENTIALS (DefaultPIN / DefaultPUK / DefaultManagementKey):

piv.go declares the PIV applet default credentials as package variables: PIN
"123456", PUK "12345678", and a 24-byte management key of 01..08 repeated three
times. Credential scanners flag them as hardcoded secrets (CWE-798). They are
upstream's and are carried unchanged: that var block is byte-identical to
piv/piv.go lines 31-45 of go-piv/piv-go/v2 v2.5.0, and the same block is
unchanged in v2.6.0.

No code reads them. Running

    grep -rn -E "Default(PIN|PUK|ManagementKey)" .

from plugins/signers/piv returns the declaration plus six comment lines and
nothing else. Three of those comments are upstream's own usage examples passing
a default as the OLD argument to SetManagementKey / SetPIN / SetPUK, i.e. the
value being replaced.

Nor can anything reach them. The PIN is supplied only by a PINPrompter:
Card.Signer in ../../piv.go returns an error when no prompter is configured, and
InteractivePINPrompt in ../../prompt.go refuses a non-TTY stdin, so a default
cannot stand in for a user-entered PIN. No file outside this directory mentions
ManagementKey at all, and authManagementKey here is unexported with no caller
anywhere in the module.

TestVendoredDefaultCredentialsAreNeverUsed in ../../piv_test.go holds the "no
code reads them" half of that: it walks every .go file outside internal/vendored
and fails if any of the three identifiers appears.

Keep the block as upstream writes it. Editing these lines to quiet a scanner
would desynchronize this directory from upstream and buy no security: the
identical bytes are published in go-piv/piv-go's public Apache-2.0 source.
